WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:02.752
There you are.

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:04.129
Who doesn’t love dogs?

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.047
Golden Retrievers.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.424
Chocolate Lab.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:08.842
A German Shepard. 

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:10.092
A Yorkie.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:11.135
Pugs.

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:12.178
Jack Russell.

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:13.596
What else?

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:14.931
And a Boxer.

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:17.517
Oh, we’ve got a lot of dogs.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.146
Puppy Place is about two kids, 

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:22.856
Lizzie and Charles, 

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:26.026
who fall into the joys of fostering dogs.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.986
A puppy!

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.572
They try to find dogs homes

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:32.282
and have to deal with different situations 

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:33.658
that come with fostering dogs.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:35.452
This truly is a dream come true.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:36.453
Hahaha.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:37.120
No, I'm serious.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.455
I actually dreamed about it.

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:40.832
I’ve been a dog person my whole life.

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:42.917
Dogs, everything else.

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:45.795
Each book for us is really a jumping off point.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:48.131
Sixty-five books with more coming.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.966
So I was like, “This is fantastic."

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:51.342
I promise.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.386
It’s specifically about the children

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.804
and how they are learning life lessons,

00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:56.973
learning responsibility, 

00:00:56.973 --> 00:00:59.059
and the way they do that is through their friendships

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.935
and through fostering 

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:02.145
and re-homing dogs.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:02.979
Trust me.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:03.897
We can handle it. 

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:04.898
Lizzie’s very smart

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.274
and determined

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:07.650
and she knows everything 

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.902
and anything about dogs.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.861
You know more about dogs 

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:10.945
than most adults I’ve worked with.

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:12.781
Charles is

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.240
a problem solver.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.076
He always tries to help the dogs.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.118
I'm putting him in the crate. 

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:18.787
It'll help him get comfortable 

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.246
in his new environment.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.915
Tucking him in like we used to do with you, 

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.209
except Jack’s not asking for a little more screen time.

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:26.294
Real funny, Dad.

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:27.796
They put everyone else’s needs 

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:28.671
before their own.

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:31.007
This is Princess, our new foster puppy. 

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:32.050
Your son

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.301
is my hero.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:35.762
We have a different dog every episode.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.180
So with these dogs, 

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:38.556
Lizzie and Charles try to find 

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:41.142
people who mostly match the dogs

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:42.852
and dogs that mostly

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:43.895
match the people.

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:44.896
I don’t think we’re a match. 

00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:46.356
Seems too

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:48.608
elegant, and I'm a man of the people.

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.320
What do you think I love about playing Lizzie?

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.363
The dogs!

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:55.657
I grew up with dogs.

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.283
Dogs are awesome.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.910
Just full of love.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:01:59.452
Dogs comfort us.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.537
We came to cheer you up. 

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:01.788
They're loyal.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.958
They kind of do everything we need for us 

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.084
without asking much in return.

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:07.168
I'm ready for my lunch.

00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:10.672
 

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:13.007
One of the most rewarding parts of doing the show is that

00:02:13.007 --> 00:02:14.175
the cast and crew 

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:15.718
get to adopt the dogs.

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:17.512
And it’s really cool because 

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:18.304
sometimes when they adopt dogs 

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.764
we get to see them again.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.850
Totally.

00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:23.935
Local residents in nearby businesses…

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:25.228
I really hope Dad's okay.

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:27.105
Well, he could certainly use a hot shower.

00:02:27.105 --> 00:02:27.939
Dad!

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:29.440
I think one of the biggest lessons is 

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.025
family comes first and

00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:31.776
we all need each other.

00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:34.028
Mm-mm-mm.

00:02:34.028 --> 00:02:35.113
Doing this felt good

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:37.073
and I think when people watch it

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.199
they’ll be able to feel good watching it.

00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:39.492
It's also really cool 

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.202
to be a part of a show that has 

00:02:41.202 --> 00:02:42.453
such a great message about 

00:02:42.453 --> 00:02:43.496
rescuing dogs.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.247
We did it!

00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.623
Yes!

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:49.419
We want people to think about

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:50.003
animal rescue, 

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.504
animal fostering.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.506
And if you like dogs, then it's a good

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.424
show for you to watch.

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:56.634
It's fun, and it's organic, 

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.679
and it has honestly been the most fulfilling experience

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.638
of my life.

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:01.639
That's

00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:03.266
Puppy Place in a nutshell.

